course: dictionary
lesson: 7713
title: Working out a word from its context
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: You can often work out a new word from the words around it. «A pterosaur wing was skin stretched from a very long fourth finger.» The words wing and skin tell you that a pterosaur was an animal that could fly.
explain: Some sentences give you a clear meaning. «Pterosaurs, often called pterodactyls, were flying reptiles, close cousins of dinosaurs but not dinosaurs.» The sentence tells you what a pterosaur was: a flying reptile, related to dinosaurs but not one of them.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «A pterosaur was a flying reptile» still makes sense, so your meaning fits the text.
fact: A pterosaur was a flying reptile that lived at the time of the dinosaurs.
fact: Pterosaurs were not dinosaurs and not birds; they were close cousins of dinosaurs.
fact: A pterosaur's wing was skin stretched from one very long fourth finger.
fact: The largest pterosaurs, such as Quetzalcoatlus, had wings about 10 metres across.
fact: Pterosaurs died out with the dinosaurs.
exercise: «A pterosaur wing was skin stretched from a very long fourth finger.» What was a pterosaur's wing made of? | Thin metal bones | Leaves from the trees | *Skin stretched from a long finger | Feathers from a bird
exercise: What kind of animal was a pterosaur? | A bird that lived in the sea | A fish with fins | A dinosaur with feathers | *A flying reptile
exercise: «Pterosaurs are not dinosaurs and not birds.» Based on the sentence, which is true? | Pterosaurs were a kind of bird | Pterosaurs were dinosaurs | Pterosaurs lived after the dinosaurs died out | *Pterosaurs were close cousins of dinosaurs
test: When did pterosaurs live? | In the ice age | Only in the future | Today, in deserts | *At the time of the dinosaurs
test: «The biggest pterosaur, Quetzalcoatlus, had wings about 10 metres across.» What does this tell you? | Pterosaurs had no wings | *Some pterosaurs were huge | Pterosaurs were tiny | Pterosaurs were the same size as birds
exam: What is the best meaning of pterosaur, using the clues in the sentences? | A small bird that sings | A mammal that lived in trees | A dinosaur that swam in the sea | *A flying reptile from the time of the dinosaurs
